//! The WIT's value types as plain Rust, with no dependency on the engine or wasmtime: each at
//! the path the engine's `bindgen!` gives it, `<namespace>::<package>::<interface>::<Name>`,
//! flags a struct of `bool`s, and the engine converts each to its own with `From`. Of the
//! interfaces the engine's world imports, those whose Rust types the engine takes from another
//! crate, `wasdk:gpu`'s and WASI's, are not here.
//!
//! Generated by `cargo xtask sync-wit` from `wit/` (`xtask/src/wit_types`): nothing edits it.
//!
//! Left out, as each holds a resource, a stream or a future, which a plain value cannot:
//!
//! - `wasdk:platform/screens.screen-change`
//! - `wasdk:platform/clipboard.content`
//! - `wasdk:platform/views.placed-layer`
//! - `wasdk:platform/views.view-change`
//! - `wasdk:platform/views.key-input`
//! - `wasdk:platform/views.view-event`
//! - `wasdk:platform/fonts.font-file`
//! - `wasdk:platform/gpu-interop.texture-plane`
//! - `wasdk:media/video-frames.video-output`
//! - `wasdk:media/media-players.video-output`
//!
//! Left out, as each holds a type of `wasdk:gpu` or WASI, which is not here:
//!
//! - `wasdk:platform/system.instant`
//! - `wasdk:platform/notifications.instant`
//! - `wasdk:platform/file-watching.error-code`
//! - `wasdk:platform/mounts.error-code`
//! - `wasdk:platform/gpu-interop.texture-aspect`

